Ladybird adds a clear button to the editable search field and exposes it
through the prefixed search-cancel-button pseudo-element.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37 and WebKit 26.5 cleared a focused search input on a
pointer click at its inline end, including in right-to-left text. Both
dispatched an input Event and a change Event on blur. Chrome also
dispatched the nonstandard search event.

Blink clears the value in
SearchFieldCancelButtonElement::DefaultEventHandler(). WebKit creates
the clear button in TextControlInnerElements.cpp. Gecko gates the
anonymous button in TextControlElement.cpp. Firefox 151.0 left the value
intact in its default configuration.
